  "id": "Compound::DB00172 - Gene::65263",
  "verbalization": "L-proline exhibits a complex interaction with Pycrl, as evidenced by multiple pathways linking it to this protein. The core mechanism appears to involve L-proline binding to Pycr2, which then participates in various metabolic processes, including the reduction of pyrroline-5-carboxylate and the oxidation of the ch-nh group. These activities are ultimately linked to Pycrl, suggesting a role in the regulation of these metabolic pathways. The evidence supports a dependency on L-proline for the function of Pycrl, as L-proline is involved in both biosynthetic and redox processes that are critical for Pycrl's activity. The overlapping participation of Pycr2 in multiple pathways indicates that L-proline may influence Pycrl through a shared regulatory network, potentially modulating its function in metabolic processes.",
